WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:02.435 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest tonight
is a United States Senator
from Vermont

00:00:02.435 --> 00:00:04.304 align:start size:94% position:6%
and former
Presidential candidate.

00:00:04.304 --> 00:00:07.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome back to the sho
Senator Bernie Sanders.

00:00:07.774 --> 00:00:10.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
Welcome back to the show,
Senator. How are you?

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm great.
Good to be with you.

00:00:12.278 --> 00:00:15.849
-You were our first
quarantined guest on March 30th,

00:00:15.849 --> 00:00:19.719
and I really hoped the next time
we talked it would be in person.

00:00:19.719 --> 00:00:23.123
But I do appreciate you
making time for us again.

00:00:23.123 --> 00:00:23.690 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
How are you --

00:00:23.690 --> 00:00:27.327
I know you're a man who like
to be around your constituents

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:28.161 line:92%
You like to be around people

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:32.532
How are you getting throug
this telephone/Zoom era?

00:00:32.532 --> 00:00:35.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would be being dishones
with you

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.570 size:75% position:38%
if I didn't tell you
that it's difficult.

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.374 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, I thrive
and I get my oxygen

00:00:41.374 --> 00:00:42.909 line:92%
from being around people.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:45.945 align:start size:94% position:6%
I miss being in
the kind of physical contact

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would like to be
with my grandchildren.

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.750 line:92%
So, it's hard, but, you know

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:52.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
we're doing the best
that we can do.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:57.157 size:81% position:41%
-You have been through
many protest movements

00:00:57.157 --> 00:01:00.860 align:start size:94% position:6%
in your long career
as an activist.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:03.830 size:75% position:38%
What is your take on
the protest movement

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.398 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we're going through
right now?

00:01:05.398 --> 00:01:10.703
Is it as Earth-changing
as many are saying it is?

00:01:10.703 --> 00:01:11.971 size:84% position:42% line:92%
-It is a very big deal.

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:15.875 align:start size:94% position:6%
It is really unprecedented
and it's extraordinary

00:01:15.875 --> 00:01:20.413
and especially taking plac
in the midst of the pandemic

00:01:20.413 --> 00:01:21.815 size:84% position:42% line:92%
And what you are seeing

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:23.783 align:start size:94% position:6%
in large cities
all over the country

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:25.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
and in small towns
is people saying,

00:01:25.952 --> 00:01:27.320 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
"Enough is enough,"

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.024 align:start size:94% position:6%
to police brutality
and police murder,

00:01:31.024 --> 00:01:32.125 size:84% position:42% line:92%
that we have to rethink

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
the whole nature of policing
in America,

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:38.698 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have to deal
with institutional racism.

00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:41.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And that is just
an extraordinary moment

00:01:41.768 --> 00:01:43.169 line:92%
in our country's history.

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:46.372 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You have clarified
that you are not for

00:01:46.372 --> 00:01:47.107 size:81% position:41% line:92%
abolishing the police,

00:01:47.107 --> 00:01:51.845
which a lot of people assume
"defunding the police" means

00:01:51.845 --> 00:01:55.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
Where are you
on that sliding scale

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:58.184 align:start size:94% position:6%
between the idea of no polic
and --

00:01:58.184 --> 00:01:59.052 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-I don't think --

00:01:59.052 --> 00:02:00.320
Seth, I don't think that,
at the end of the day,

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:04.824 align:start size:94% position:6%
most people think we should no
have any police department
in America.

00:02:04.824 --> 00:02:07.827 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I think what most people
think is

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:10.663 line:92%
we have to reallocate resource

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:13.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
and rethink the function
of policing.

00:02:13.766 --> 00:02:17.137 size:84% position:42%
Obviously, for a start,
we have to do away with

00:02:17.137 --> 00:02:20.039 align:start size:94% position:6%
police murders
and police brutality.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.407 line:92%
That goes without saying.

00:02:21.407 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the other thing that
I think we have to do

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:25.945 size:75% position:38% line:92%
is to ask ourselves,

00:02:25.945 --> 00:02:29.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Should police be forced
to deal every day

00:02:29.916 --> 00:02:34.020
with issues like mental illness,
drug addiction,

00:02:34.020 --> 00:02:36.289 align:start size:94% position:6%
alcohol addiction,
homelessness?"

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:39.025 size:88% position:44%
Police spend a whole lot
of their time and energy

00:02:39.025 --> 00:02:43.196 align:start size:94% position:6%
doing things that they are not
necessarily trained to do

00:02:43.196 --> 00:02:46.366 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that take
a lot of resources.

00:02:46.366 --> 00:02:47.700 line:92%
So I think what people wan

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:52.739
when we talk about defunding the
police or reallocating resources

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:57.243 align:start size:94% position:6%
is also to put money into
the causes of crime.

00:02:57.243 --> 00:03:01.381
Why do we have more people i
jail than any other country?

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
Should we be
legalizing marijuana,

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.852 line:92%
which, in my view, we should

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:09.489 size:81% position:41%
Should we be investing
in jobs and education

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:12.258 align:start size:94% position:6%
rather than just locking u
more and more people?

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:18.031
So I think this moment makes u
rethink the function of policing

00:03:18.031 --> 00:03:20.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the reallocation
of resources,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.801 align:start size:94% position:6%
something I very strongly
believe in.

00:03:21.801 --> 00:03:25.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-President Trump today
signed some executive orders

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:26.206 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
on police reform.

00:03:26.206 --> 00:03:29.542 align:start size:94% position:6%
And even, you know, Democratic
leadership over the years

00:03:29.542 --> 00:03:31.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
has called for reforms
like body cameras,

00:03:31.844 --> 00:03:33.379 line:92%
like anti-bias trainings.

00:03:33.379 --> 00:03:39.485
Does the President's steps today
make you optimistic?

00:03:39.485 --> 00:03:43.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or do you feel like they are
short of what we need?

00:03:43.456 --> 00:03:46.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, Seth, we're short
of what we need.

00:03:46.459 --> 00:03:48.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we are working
in the Senate,

00:03:48.761 --> 00:03:51.631 size:78% position:39%
and I have introduced
a set of proposals

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.967 line:92%
which go a lot, a lot further.

00:03:53.967 --> 00:03:56.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, the bottom line here
is that

00:03:56.502 --> 00:04:01.040
police officers need to be hel
accountable for their actions.

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.611
And that's something that ha
not taken place in the past.

00:04:04.611 --> 00:04:08.348
We need to make sure that police
departments around the country

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:12.852 align:start size:94% position:6%
receive the training to
understand that lethal force

00:04:12.852 --> 00:04:16.956 align:start size:94% position:6%
shooting somebody,
is a last response,

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:19.158 size:78% position:39% line:92%
not a first response.

00:04:19.158 --> 00:04:23.162
So there are a whole number of
things that have got to be done.

00:04:23.162 --> 00:04:24.864 line:92%
I think Trump is responding from

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
the pressure
of the American people.

00:04:26.899 --> 00:04:29.102 align:start size:94% position:6%
Not just Democrats
or independents.

00:04:29.102 --> 00:04:29.936 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Republicans, as well.

00:04:29.936 --> 00:04:33.640
But we have to go a lot furthe
than Trump is talking about.

00:04:33.640 --> 00:04:35.041 line:92%
-Another thing, I imagine,

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:37.377 size:84% position:42%
you feel the government
needs to go further on

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:40.313
is how we're taking care o
people during this pandemic.

00:04:40.313 --> 00:04:42.682 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously,
Congress has passed some bills

00:04:42.682 --> 00:04:44.784 size:88% position:44%
It's been a while since
they passed another one.

00:04:44.784 --> 00:04:46.486 align:start size:94% position:6%
What steps need to be take
moving forward?

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:49.055
Because, obviously, things
like unemployment insuranc

00:04:49.055 --> 00:04:50.189 line:92%
aren't gonna go on forever

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:54.060 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we can see a real spik
in what people need,

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:54.761 size:81% position:41% line:92%
not just in the virus,

00:04:54.761 --> 00:04:57.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
but insofar as what people nee
from the government.

00:04:57.930 --> 00:04:59.766 line:92%
-Well, Seth, I would hope that

00:04:59.766 --> 00:05:02.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
out of this terrible momen
in American history,

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:05.938 line:92%
which is really unprecedented --

00:05:05.938 --> 00:05:06.873 line:92%
I mean, you're looking at

00:05:06.873 --> 00:05:10.076 align:start size:94% position:6%
110,000 people dead alread
from the virus.

00:05:10.076 --> 00:05:13.479
You're looking at 30 million
people having lost their jobs.

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
You're looking at people
who have lost, by the millions

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:18.251 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
their healthcare,

00:05:18.251 --> 00:05:20.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
people unable to
pay their rents,

00:05:20.153 --> 00:05:23.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
worried about
losing their homes,

00:05:23.589 --> 00:05:25.024 line:92%
kids not being in school.

00:05:25.024 --> 00:05:27.794 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's an unprecedented moment
in American history.

00:05:27.794 --> 00:05:31.631 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I would hope that
we take this opportunity

00:05:31.631 --> 00:05:33.566 line:92%
to say and ask ourselves,

00:05:33.566 --> 00:05:36.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
"How did we get to where we ar
right now,

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:40.907
and where do we want to be
in the next couple of months

00:05:40.907 --> 00:05:41.974 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
and in the future?"

00:05:41.974 --> 00:05:43.209 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, in the next
couple of months,

00:05:43.209 --> 00:05:45.545
what we have got to do -- no
in the next couple of months

00:05:45.545 --> 00:05:47.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
the next couple of weeks,
immediately --

00:05:47.180 --> 00:05:51.084
what we have got to do is pass
what we call a "corona fall,

00:05:51.084 --> 00:05:52.652 line:92%
piece of major legislation

00:05:52.652 --> 00:05:56.255 align:start size:94% position:6%
which says that when 30 millio
people have lost their job

00:05:56.255 --> 00:05:58.191 align:start size:94% position:6%
and millions have lost
their healthcare,

00:05:58.191 --> 00:06:01.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
we have got to stand up
and protect them.

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:02.495 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Various ways to do that.

00:06:02.495 --> 00:06:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
But at the very least,
working people

00:06:04.497 --> 00:06:08.835 align:start size:94% position:6%
need to continue to get
decent unemployment checks

00:06:08.835 --> 00:06:10.436 line:92%
when unemployment is so high

00:06:10.436 --> 00:06:13.139 align:start size:94% position:6%
In my view, during the midst
of this crisis,

00:06:13.139 --> 00:06:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
while we work toward
Medicare for All,

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:16.943 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
clearly, right now,

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:20.947
everybody must be entitled t
healthcare as a human right.

00:06:20.947 --> 00:06:24.016 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that
a $1,200 one-time check

00:06:24.016 --> 00:06:26.018 line:92%
is not enough during the crisis.

00:06:26.018 --> 00:06:29.155
We should make sure that
every individual in this country

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:30.723 size:78% position:39% line:92%
gets at least $2,000.

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because so many of our peopl
are hurting.

00:06:33.426 --> 00:06:34.627 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
$2,000 a month.

00:06:34.627 --> 00:06:36.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's some of what
we got to do.

00:06:36.095 --> 00:06:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
Long-term, we have got to
ask ourselves,

00:06:39.232 --> 00:06:44.303
"How does it happen that whe
so many people lose their jobs

00:06:44.303 --> 00:06:46.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
they also lose
their healthcare?"

00:06:46.105 --> 00:06:50.109 align:start size:94% position:6%
Should healthcare in America
just be a job benefit,

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:52.178 line:92%
or should it be a human right?

00:06:52.178 --> 00:06:54.647 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, I think it should b
a human right.

00:06:54.647 --> 00:06:57.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
I hope more and more peopl
understand that.

00:06:57.550 --> 00:07:00.453 align:start size:94% position:6%
Second of all,
before the pandemic,

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:01.754 line:92%
we had Trump, as you all recall,

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:03.923 align:start size:94% position:6%
telling us what a great econom
we had.

00:07:03.923 --> 00:07:07.627 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, how great is an econom
when half of our people

00:07:07.627 --> 00:07:09.195 line:92%
are living paycheck to paychec

00:07:09.195 --> 00:07:13.733
and, when the paychecks stop
hunger and desperation set in?

00:07:13.733 --> 00:07:15.568 line:92%
So we have got to make sur

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:18.104 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we raise the minimum wage
in this country

00:07:18.104 --> 00:07:20.139 line:92%
to at least 15 bucks an hour

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:23.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
make it easier for workers
to join unions.

00:07:23.776 --> 00:07:25.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, we have got to
make sure that all of our kids

00:07:25.978 --> 00:07:27.914 align:start size:94% position:6%
get the quality education
that they need.

00:07:27.914 --> 00:07:29.582 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what I'm saying, Seth,
is that

00:07:29.582 --> 00:07:32.351 size:84% position:42%
in this terrible moment
in American history,

00:07:32.351 --> 00:07:35.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
when so many of our people
are hurting,

00:07:35.321 --> 00:07:36.522 size:78% position:39% line:92%
it is time to rethink

00:07:36.522 --> 00:07:40.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of the basic priorities
of our nation,

00:07:40.193 --> 00:07:43.629 align:start size:94% position:6%
some of the basic institutions
in this country,

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:45.598 align:start size:94% position:6%
and, as the wealthiest country
on Earth,

00:07:45.598 --> 00:07:48.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
ask ourselves where we want to
be in the future.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We'll be right back
with more of my conversation

00:07:51.070 --> 00:07:53.539 line:92%
with Senator Bernie Sanders.

